  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**:\n\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Download Python (python.org/downloads)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**\n\n### What is the latest version?\nThe latest stable release of Python is **Python 3.14.5**. \n\n### How to Install on Different Operating Systems:\n\n*   **Windows:** \n    *   When you visit the downloads page, it will automatically detect your OS and show a download button for Windows.\n    *   *Note:* Python also provides the **Python Install Manager** for Windows. You can download this from the official site or via the Microsoft Store to easily install, manage, and launch multiple Python versions.\n    *   During installation, make sure to check the box that says **\"Add python.exe to PATH\"** so you can run Python easily from your Command Prompt/Terminal.\n*   **macOS:**\n    *   You can download the macOS installer package (`.pkg` file) directly from the downloads page. \n    *   Alternatively, many macOS developers prefer installing Python using a package manager like [Homebrew](https://brew.sh/) by running `brew install python` in the Terminal.\n*   **Linux/Unix:**\n    *   Most Linux distributions come with Python pre-installed. \n    *   If you need to upgrade, it is highly recommended to use your distribution's package manager (e.g., `sudo apt update && sudo apt install python3` on Ubuntu/Debian) rather than compiling from source, to avoid breaking system dependencies.",
